    {
      "id": "CORE-CFG-ENVCONFIG-01",
      "title": "With no -config option, sfc-main reads its configuration from the SFC_CONFIG environment variable",
      "tier": "core",
      "priority": "P1",
      "intent": "ConfigProviderFactory falls back to EnvConfigProvider when the command line has no -config (ConfigProviderFactory.kt:53-63), the deployment form for containers. The case omits -config and puts the configuration in SFC_CONFIG; the rendered config.json says via=config-file and the variable says via=SFC_CONFIG, so every record proves which one ran. Uberjar only: the harness renders JarFiles and IPC servers into the configuration file, while SFC_CONFIG is a static case value, so in-process and IPC deployments cannot be expressed in it.",
      "pins": [
        "core/sfc-core/src/main/kotlin/com/amazonaws/sfc/service/ConfigProviderFactory.kt:53",
        "core/sfc-core/src/main/kotlin/com/amazonaws/sfc/service/ConfigProviderFactory.kt:60",
        "core/sfc-core/src/main/kotlin/com/amazonaws/sfc/service/EnvConfigProvider.kt:107"
